LIMITATIONS

You may use or modify the software only for your own internal business
purposes or for non-commercial or personal use. Your own internal business
purposes include those of your company as defined below, and each entity in
your company may use the software on that basis.

For the avoidance of doubt, running the software on your own infrastructure to
operate your own organisation is an internal business purpose, whether or not
your organisation is commercial, and whether you run it unmodified or with
changes of your own. This includes using the software to produce or to deliver
goods and services to your own customers, subject to the two paragraphs below.

Providing the software's functionality to your own customers as part of a
larger product is also an internal business purpose, but only where all of the
following are true: (a) the product provides substantial functionality of its
own, independent of the software; (b) your customers cannot reach
substantially the functionality of the software through the product; and (c)
the product is not marketed, priced or sold on the basis of functionality that
the software provides. A product whose principal value to the customer is
functionality the software provides does not satisfy (b) or (c), however it is
branded, packaged or extended. Where (a), (b) and (c) are all satisfied, you
may charge for that product, and the next paragraph does not restrict you.

Except as the preceding paragraph permits, you may distribute the software or
provide it to others only if you do so free of charge and for non-commercial
purposes. In every case, and whether or not the preceding paragraph applies,
you may not provide the software to third parties as a hosted or managed
service where the service gives them substantially the functionality of the
software.

You may not alter, remove, or obscure any licensing, copyright, or other
notices of the licensor in the software. This license grants you no rights in
the licensor's trademarks or trade dress.

You may not use the software to train, fine-tune, or otherwise improve an
artificial intelligence or machine learning model whose output competes with
the software or reproduces its functionality, whether or not that output is
itself software. Nor may you extract, mine or systematically collect the
software's structure, logic or behaviour for the purpose of building a
competing product. For the purposes of this paragraph, "competes with" means
the model or its output is offered as a substitute for the software or any
substantial part of its functionality, whether commercially or non-commercially,
and "reproduces its functionality" means the model or its output can perform
substantially the same tasks as the software in substantially the same way.


